{"id":"mahabharata-8-040","work":"mahabharata","part":8,"partName":"कर्णपर्व","partNameEn":"Karna Parva","unit":40,"title":"चत्वारिंशत्तमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 40 · Karna's great slaughter","summary":{"en":"Karna himself, surrounded by Bhima and the Panchalas, Chedis and Kekayas, fights a mighty battle and Krishna drives Arjuna's white horses into the army. Bhima and Arjuna meanwhile fight the Samshaptakas and others.","kn":"ಭೀಮ, ಪಾಂಚಾಲ, ಚೇದಿ, ಕೇಕಯರಿಂದ ಸುತ್ತುವರಿಯಲ್ಪಟ್ಟ ಕರ್ಣ ಮಹಾಯುದ್ಧ ಮಾಡುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಕೃಷ್ಣ ಅರ್ಜುನನ ಬಿಳಿ ಕುದುರೆಗಳನ್ನು ಸೈನ್ಯದೊಳಗೆ ನಡೆಸುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಭೀಮ, ಅರ್ಜುನರು ಸಂಶಪ್ತಕರು ಮತ್ತಿತರರೊಡನೆ ಹೋರಾಡುತ್ತಾರೆ.","hi":"भीम तथा पाञ्चालों, चेदियों और केकयों से घिरा कर्ण महायुद्ध करता है और कृष्ण अर्जुन के श्वेत घोड़ों को सेना में ले जाते हैं। भीम और अर्जुन संशप्तकों और अन्य से लड़ते हैं।","te":"భీముడు, పాంచాలులు, చేదులు, కేకయులచే చుట్టుముట్టబడిన కర్ణుడు మహాయుద్ధం చేస్తాడు; కృష్ణుడు అర్జునుని తెల్లని గుర్రాలను సేనలోకి నడుపుతాడు. భీముడు, అర్జునుడు సంశప్తకులు ఇతరులతో పోరాడతారు.","ta":"பீமன், பாஞ்சாலர், சேதியர், கேகயரால் சூழப்பட்ட கர்ணன் பெரும்போர் புரிய, கண்ணன் அர்ஜுனனின் வெண்குதிரைகளைப் படையுள் செலுத்துகிறார். பீமனும் அர்ஜுனனும் சம்சப்தகர் முதலியோருடன் போரிடுகின்றனர்.","ml":"ഭീമനും പാഞ്ചാലർ, ചേദികൾ, കേകയർ എന്നിവരും ചുറ്റും നിൽക്കെ കർണ്ണൻ തന്നെ ഘോരയുദ്ധം നടത്തുന്നു; അർജുനന്റെ വെള്ളക്കുതിരകളെ കൃഷ്ണൻ സേനയിലേക്ക് തെളിക്കുന്നു. ഇതിനിടെ ഭീമനും അർജുനനും സംശപ്തകരെയും മറ്റുള്ളവരെയും നേരിടുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 8.40; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Jul 29 2019","sections":[{"title":"कर्णपर्व","titleEn":"Karna Parva","verses":[{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"भीमसेनं सपाञ्चाल्यं चेदिकेकयसंवृतम् ।\nवैकर्तनः स्वयं रुद्ध्वा वारयामास सायकैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Karna, son of Vikartana, himself blocked Bhimasena, who had the Panchalas with him and was surrounded by Chedis and Kekayas, and held him off with arrows."}},{"n":2,"text":"ततस्तु चेदिकारूषान्सृञ्जयांश्च महारथान् ।\nकर्णो जघान संक्रुद्धो भीमसेनस्य पश्यतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Karna, enraged, killed the Chedis, the Karushas and the great chariot-warriors of the Srinjayas while Bhimasena looked on."}},{"n":3,"text":"भीमसेनस्ततः कर्णं विहाय रथसत्तमम् ।\nप्रययौ कौरवं सैन्यं कक्षमग्निरिव ज्वलन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Bhimasena left Karna, best of chariot-warriors, and went off against the Kaurava army, blazing like fire in a dry thicket."}},{"n":4,"text":"सूतपुत्रोऽपि समरे पाञ्चालान्केकयांस्तथा ।\nसृञ्जयांश्च महेष्वासान्निजघान सहस्रशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The charioteer's son too killed Panchalas, Kekayas and Srinjaya great archers by the thousand in the battle."}},{"n":5,"text":"संशप्तकेषु पार्थश्च कौरवेषु वृकोदरः ।\nपाञ्चालेषु तथा कर्णः क्षयं चक्रूर्महारथाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Arjuna among the Samshaptakas, Bhima among the Kauravas and Karna among the Panchalas, those great chariot-warriors, brought about destruction."}},{"n":6,"text":"ते क्षत्रिया दह्यमानास्त्रिभिस्तैः पावकोपमैः ।\nजग्मुर्विनाशं समरे राजन्दुर्मन्त्रिते तव ॥","meaning":{"en":"King, those kshatriyas, burned by these three who were like fires, went to ruin in the battle because of your evil counsel."}},{"n":7,"text":"ततो दुर्योधनः क्रुद्धो नकुलं नवभिः शरैः ।\nविव्याध भरतश्रेष्ठ चतुरश्चास्य वाजिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Duryodhana, angry, best of the Bharatas, pierced Nakula with nine arrows and his four horses too."}},{"n":8,"text":"ततः पुनरमेयात्मा तव पुत्रो जनाधिपः ।\nक्षुरेण सहदेवस्य ध्वजं चिच्छेद काञ्चनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then again your son, the immeasurable king, cut Sahadeva's golden banner with a razor-edged arrow."}},{"n":9,"text":"नकुलस्तु ततः क्रुद्धस्तव पुत्रं त्रिसप्तभिः ।\nजघान समरे राजन्सहदेवश्च पञ्चभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Nakula, angry, struck your son with seventy-three arrows in the battle, king, and Sahadeva with five."}},{"n":10,"text":"तावुभौ भरतश्रेष्ठौ श्रेष्ठौ सर्वधनुष्मताम् ।\nविव्याधोरसि संक्रुद्धः पञ्चभिः पञ्चभिः शरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Enraged, Duryodhana pierced each of those two best of the Bharatas, the best of all bowmen, in the chest with five arrows apiece."}},{"n":11,"text":"ततोऽपराभ्यां भल्लाभ्यां धनुषी समकृन्तत ।\nयमयोः प्रहसन्राजन्विव्याधैव च सप्तभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, laughing, king, he cut both their bows with two other broad-headed arrows and pierced the twins with seven."}},{"n":12,"text":"तावन्ये धनुषी श्रेष्ठे शक्रचापनिभे शुभे ।\nप्रगृह्य रेजतुः शूरौ देवपुत्रसमौ युधि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Taking up other fine, beautiful bows like Indra's rainbow, the two heroes shone in the battle like sons of the gods."}},{"n":13,"text":"ततस्तौ रभसौ युद्धे भ्रातरौ भ्रातरं नृप ।\nशरैर्ववर्षतुर्घोरैर्महामेघौ यथाचलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then those two brothers, eager in the fight, rained fearsome arrows on their brother, king, as two great clouds rain on a mountain."}},{"n":14,"text":"ततः क्रुद्धो महाराज तव पुत्रो महारथः ।\nपाण्डुपुत्रौ महेष्वासौ वारयामास पत्रिभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then your son, the great chariot-warrior, angry, great king, held back the two sons of Pandu, both great archers, with his arrows."}},{"n":15,"text":"धनुर्मण्डलमेवास्य दृश्यते युधि भारत ।\nसायकाश्चैव दृश्यन्ते निश्चरन्तः समन्ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bharata, in the battle only the circle of his bow was seen, and arrows were seen darting out on every side."}},{"n":16,"text":"तस्य सायकसंछन्नौ चकाशेतां च पाण्डवौ ।\nमेघच्छन्नौ यथा व्योम्नि चन्द्रसूर्यौ हतप्रभौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Covered by his arrows, the two Pandavas shone dimly, like the sun and the moon in the sky when hidden by clouds and robbed of their light."}},{"n":17,"text":"ते तु बाणा महाराज हेमपुङ्खाः शिलाशिताः ।\nआच्छादयन्दिशः सर्वाः सूर्यस्येवांशवस्तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Great king, those arrows with golden feathers, sharpened on stone, covered all directions then, like the rays of the sun."}},{"n":18,"text":"बाणभूते ततस्तस्मिन्संछन्ने च नभस्तले ।\nयमाभ्यां ददृशे रूपं कालान्तकयमोपमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the sky was covered and made of arrows, the twins saw his form like that of Time, the Ender and Yama."}},{"n":19,"text":"पराक्रमं तु तं दृष्ट्वा तव सूनोर्महारथाः ।\nमृत्योरुपान्तिकं प्राप्तौ माद्रीपुत्रौ स्म मेनिरे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing that valour of your son, the great chariot-warriors thought the two sons of Madri had come to the brink of death."}},{"n":20,"text":"ततः सेनापती राजन्पाण्डवस्य महात्मनः ।\nपार्षतः प्रययौ तत्र यत्र राजा सुयोधनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, king, Dhrishtadyumna, son of Prishata, the commander of the great-souled Pandava, went to where King Suyodhana was."}},{"n":21,"text":"माद्रीपुत्रौ ततः शूरौ व्यतिक्रम्य महारथौ ।\nधृष्टद्युम्नस्तव सुतं ताडयामास सायकैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Passing by the two heroic great chariot-warriors, the sons of Madri, Dhrishtadyumna struck your son with arrows."}},{"n":22,"text":"तमविध्यदमेयात्मा तव पुत्रोऽत्यमर्षणः ।\nपाञ्चाल्यं पञ्चविंशत्या प्रहस्य पुरुषर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Your son, of immeasurable spirit and very intolerant, laughed, bull among men, and pierced the Panchala prince with twenty-five arrows."}},{"n":23,"text":"ततः पुनरमेयात्मा पुत्रस्ते पृथिवीपते ।\nविद्ध्वा ननाद पाञ्चाल्यं षष्ट्या पञ्चभिरेव च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, lord of the earth, your immeasurable son again pierced the Panchala with sixty-five and roared."}},{"n":24,"text":"अथास्य सशरं चापं हस्तावापं च मारिष ।\nक्षुरप्रेण सुतीक्ष्णेन राजा चिच्छेद संयुगे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, lord, the king cut his bow with its arrow and the arm-guard on his hand with a very sharp razor-edged arrow in the battle."}},{"n":25,"text":"तदपास्य धनुश्छिन्नं पाञ्चाल्यः शत्रुकर्शनः ।\nअन्यदादत्त वेगेन धनुर्भारसहं नवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Throwing aside that cut bow, the Panchala, scorcher of enemies, quickly took up another new bow that could bear the strain."}},{"n":26,"text":"प्रज्वलन्निव वेगेन संरम्भाद्रुधिरेक्षणः ।\nअशोभत महेष्वासो धृष्टद्युम्नः कृतव्रणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Wounded, with eyes red from fury, as though blazing with speed, the great archer Dhrishtadyumna shone."}},{"n":27,"text":"स पञ्चदश नाराचाञ्श्वसतः पन्नगानिव ।\nजिघांसुर्भरतश्रेष्ठं धृष्टद्युम्नो व्यवासृजत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Wishing to kill the best of the Bharatas, Dhrishtadyumna loosed fifteen iron arrows that hissed like snakes."}},{"n":28,"text":"ते वर्म हेमविकृतं भित्त्वा राज्ञः शिलाशिताः ।\nविविशुर्वसुधां वेगात्कङ्कबर्हिणवाससः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those stone-sharpened arrows, fletched with heron and peacock feathers, pierced the king's gold-wrought armour and plunged swiftly into the earth."}},{"n":29,"text":"सोऽतिविद्धो महाराज पुत्रस्तेऽतिव्यराजत ।\nवसन्ते पुष्पशबलः सपुष्प इव किंशुकः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Greatly pierced, great king, your son shone brightly, like a flowering kimshuka tree in spring, mottled with blossom."}},{"n":30,"text":"स छिन्नवर्मा नाराचैः प्रहारैर्जर्जरच्छविः ।\nधृष्टद्युम्नस्य भल्लेन क्रुद्धश्चिच्छेद कार्मुकम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"With armour cut, his body battered by the blows of iron arrows, he angrily cut Dhrishtadyumna's bow with a broad-headed arrow."}},{"n":31,"text":"अथैनं छिन्नधन्वानं त्वरमाणो महीपतिः ।\nसायकैर्दशभी राजन्भ्रुवोर्मध्ये समार्दयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, king, hurrying, the lord of the earth struck the son of Prishata, whose bow was cut, between the eyebrows with ten arrows."}},{"n":32,"text":"तस्य तेऽशोभयन्वक्त्रं कर्मारपरिमार्जिताः ।\nप्रफुल्लं चम्पकं यद्वद्भ्रमरा मधुलिप्सवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those arrows, polished by the smith, adorned his face as bees eager for honey adorn a blooming champaka."}},{"n":33,"text":"तदपास्य धनुश्छिन्नं धृष्टद्युम्नो महामनाः ।\nअन्यदादत्त वेगेन धनुर्भल्लांश्च षोडश ॥","meaning":{"en":"Throwing aside that cut bow, the great-minded Dhrishtadyumna quickly took another bow and sixteen broad-headed arrows."}},{"n":34,"text":"ततो दुर्योधनस्याश्वान्हत्वा सूतं च पञ्चभिः ।\nधनुश्चिच्छेद भल्लेन जातरूपपरिष्कृतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then he killed Duryodhana's horses and his charioteer with five arrows, and cut his bow decorated with gold with another arrow."}},{"n":35,"text":"रथं सोपस्करं छत्रं शक्तिं खड्गं गदां ध्वजम् ।\nभल्लैश्चिच्छेद नवभिः पुत्रस्य तव पार्षतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"With nine broad-headed arrows the son of Prishata cut your son's chariot with its equipment, his umbrella, spear, sword, mace and banner."}},{"n":36,"text":"तपनीयाङ्गदं चित्रं नागं मणिमयं शुभम् ।\nध्वजं कुरुपतेश्छिन्नं ददृशुः सर्वपार्थिवाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"All the kings saw the Kuru lord's banner cut down, the beautiful elephant emblem set with jewels and with golden armlets."}},{"n":37,"text":"दुर्योधनं तु विरथं छिन्नसर्वायुधं रणे ।\nभ्रातरः पर्यरक्षन्त सोदर्या भरतर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"With Duryodhana left chariotless and all his weapons cut, bull of the Bharatas, his brothers of the same womb protected him in the battle."}},{"n":38,"text":"तमारोप्य रथे राजन्दण्डधारो जनाधिपम् ।\nअपोवाह च संभ्रान्तो धृष्टद्युम्नस्य पश्यतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"King, Dandadhara took the lord of the people up onto his chariot and carried him away in confusion, while Dhrishtadyumna looked on."}},{"n":39,"text":"कर्णस्तु सात्यकिं जित्वा राजगृद्धी महाबलः ।\nद्रोणहन्तारमुग्रेषुं ससाराभिमुखं रणे ॥","meaning":{"en":"But mighty Karna, having defeated Satyaki, eager for the king's cause, went in the battle toward his opponent, the slayer of Drona, whose arrows were fierce."}},{"n":40,"text":"तं पृष्ठतोऽभ्ययात्तूर्णं शैनेयो वितुदञ्शरैः ।\nवारणं जघनोपान्ते विषाणाभ्यामिव द्विपः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Satyaki, the Shaineya, followed swiftly from behind, tormenting Karna with arrows, like an elephant goaded by tusks at its hindquarters."}},{"n":41,"text":"स भारत महानासीद्योधानां सुमहात्मनाम् ।\nकर्णपार्षतयोर्मध्ये त्वदीयानां महारणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bharata, there was a great battle there of your great-souled warriors between Karna and the son of Prishata."}},{"n":42,"text":"न पाण्डवानां नास्माकं योधः कश्चित्पराङ्मुखः ।\nप्रत्यदृश्यत यत्कर्णः पाञ्चालांस्त्वरितो ययौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"No warrior of the Pandavas or of ours was seen turning his back, because Karna was going swiftly at the Panchalas."}},{"n":43,"text":"तस्मिन्क्षणे नरश्रेष्ठ गजवाजिनरक्षयः ।\nप्रादुरासीदुभयतो राजन्मध्यंगतेऽहनि ॥","meaning":{"en":"At that moment, best of men, a destruction of elephants, horses and men appeared on both sides as the day reached its midpoint."}},{"n":44,"text":"पाञ्चालास्तु महाराज त्वरिता विजिगीषवः ।\nसर्वतोऽभ्यद्रवन्कर्णं पतत्रिण इव द्रुमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Great king, the Panchalas, hurrying and eager for victory, rushed from every side at Karna like birds at a tree."}},{"n":45,"text":"तेषामाधिरथिः क्रुद्धो यतमानान्मनस्विनः ।\nविचिन्वन्नेव बाणाग्रैः समासादयदग्रतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Karna, the son of Adhiratha, angry, as those proud men strove, met them one by one in front, picking them out with the points of his arrows."}},{"n":46,"text":"व्याघ्रकेतुं सुशर्माणं शङ्कुं चोग्रं धनंजयम् ।\nशुक्लं च रोचमानं च सिंहसेनं च दुर्जयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He struck Vyaghraketu, Susharma, Shanku, Ugra, Dhananjaya, Shukla, Rochamana and the unconquerable Simhasena."}},{"n":47,"text":"ते वीरा रथवेगेन परिवव्रुर्नरोत्तमम् ।\nसृजन्तं सायकान्क्रुद्धं कर्णमाहवशोभिनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those heroes, with the speed of their chariots, surrounded that best of men, Karna, angry and shining in battle as he loosed arrows."}},{"n":48,"text":"युध्यमानांस्तु ताञ्शूरान्मनुजेन्द्रः प्रतापवान् ।\nअष्टाभिरष्टौ राधेयो न्यहनन्निशितैः शरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The mighty lord of men, Radheya, killed those eight heroes as they fought, with eight sharp arrows."}},{"n":49,"text":"अथापरान्महाराज सूतपुत्रः प्रतापवान् ।\nजघान बहुसाहस्रान्योधान्युद्धविशारदः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, great king, the mighty charioteer's son, skilled in fighting, killed thousands more warriors."}},{"n":50,"text":"विष्णुं च विष्णुकर्माणं देवापिं भद्रमेव च ।\nदण्डं च समरे राजंश्चित्रं चित्रायुधं हरिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"King, in the battle he killed Vishnu, Vishnukarma, Devapi, Bhadra, Danda, Chitra, Chitrayudha and Hari."}},{"n":51,"text":"सिंहकेतुं रोचमानं शलभं च महारथम् ।\nनिजघान सुसंक्रुद्धश्चेदीनां च महारथान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Greatly angered, he also killed Simhaketu, Rochamana, the great chariot-warrior Shalabha and the great chariot-warriors of the Chedis."}},{"n":52,"text":"तेषामाददतः प्राणानासीदाधिरथेर्वपुः ।\nशोणिताभ्युक्षिताङ्गस्य रुद्रस्येवोर्जितं महत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As he took their lives, the body of Adhiratha's son, with limbs sprinkled in blood, appeared mighty like that of Rudra."}},{"n":53,"text":"तत्र भारत कर्णेन मातङ्गास्ताडिताः शरैः ।\nसर्वतोऽभ्यद्रवन्भीताः कुर्वन्तो महदाकुलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bharata, elephants struck there by Karna's arrows fled from every side in fear, causing great confusion."}},{"n":54,"text":"निपेतुरुर्व्यां समरे कर्णसायकपीडिताः ।\nकुर्वन्तो विविधान्नादान्वज्रनुन्ना इवाचलाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Tormented by Karna's arrows they fell to the ground in the battle, crying out in many ways, like mountains struck by the thunderbolt."}},{"n":55,"text":"गजवाजिमनुष्यैश्च निपतद्भिः समन्ततः ।\nरथैश्चावगतैर्मार्गे पर्यस्तीर्यत मेदिनी ॥","meaning":{"en":"With elephants, horses and men falling on every side and chariots lying broken on the roads, the earth was strewn over."}},{"n":56,"text":"नैव भीष्मो न च द्रोणो नाप्यन्ये युधि तावकाः ।\nचक्रुः स्म तादृशं कर्म यादृशं वै कृतं रणे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Neither Bhishma nor Drona nor any other of your warriors did in the battle such a deed as was done there."}},{"n":57,"text":"सूतपुत्रेण नागेषु रथेषु च हयेषु च ।\nनरेषु च नरव्याघ्र कृतं स्म कदनं महत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Tiger among men, the charioteer's son wrought great slaughter among elephants, chariots, horses and men."}},{"n":58,"text":"मृगमध्ये यथा सिंहो दृश्यते निर्भयश्चरन् ।\nपाञ्चालानां तथा मध्ये कर्णोऽचरदभीतवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As a lion is seen moving fearless among deer, so Karna moved among the Panchalas without fear."}},{"n":59,"text":"यथा मृगगणांस्त्रस्तान्सिंहो द्रावयते दिशः ।\nपाञ्चालानां रथव्रातान्कर्णो द्रावयते तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"As a lion scatters frightened herds of deer in all directions, so Karna scattered the Panchalas' bands of chariots."}},{"n":60,"text":"सिंहास्यं च यथा प्राप्य न जीवन्ति मृगाः क्वचित् ।\nतथा कर्णमनुप्राप्य न जीवन्ति महारथाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As deer that fall into a lion's mouth never live, so great chariot-warriors who came upon Karna did not live."}},{"n":61,"text":"वैश्वानरं यथा दीप्तं दह्यन्ते प्राप्य वै जनाः ।\nकर्णाग्निना रणे तद्वद्दग्धा भारत सृञ्जयाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As people who reach a blazing fire are burned, so, Bharata, the Srinjayas were burned in the battle by the fire of Karna."}},{"n":62,"text":"कर्णेन चेदिष्वेकेन पाञ्चालेषु च भारत ।\nविश्राव्य नाम निहता बहवः शूरसंमताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bharata, Karna alone killed many esteemed heroes among the Chedis and Panchalas, after announcing their names."}},{"n":63,"text":"मम चासीन्मनुष्येन्द्र दृष्ट्वा कर्णस्य विक्रमम् ।\nनैकोऽप्याधिरथेर्जीवन्पाञ्चाल्यो मोक्ष्यते युधि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Lord of men, seeing Karna's prowess I thought that not a single Panchala would escape from the son of Adhiratha alive in the battle."}},{"n":64,"text":"पाञ्चालान्विधमन्संख्ये सूतपुत्रः प्रतापवान् ।\nअभ्यधावत संक्रुद्धो धर्मपुत्रं युधिष्ठिरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Destroying the Panchalas in the fight, the mighty charioteer's son, in a rage, ran at Yudhishthira, son of Dharma."}},{"n":65,"text":"धृष्टद्युम्नश्च राजानं द्रौपदेयाश्च मारिष ।\nपरिवव्रुरमित्रघ्नं शतशश्चापरे जनाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Lord, Dhrishtadyumna and the sons of Draupadi, and hundreds of others, surrounded the king, the destroyer of enemies."}},{"n":66,"text":"शिखण्डी सहदेवश्च नकुलो नाकुलिस्तथा ।\nजनमेजयः शिनेर्नप्ता बहवश्च प्रभद्रकाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shikhandi, Sahadeva, Nakula, Nakula's son, Janamejaya, Shini's grandson Satyaki and many Prabhadrakas did the same."}},{"n":67,"text":"एते पुरोगमा भूत्वा धृष्टद्युम्नस्य संयुगे ।\nकर्णमस्यन्तमिष्वस्त्रैर्विचेरुरमितौजसः ॥","meaning":{"en":"These, becoming the leaders under Dhrishtadyumna in the battle, men of boundless vigour, moved about Karna as he shot with his bows and weapons."}},{"n":68,"text":"तांस्तत्राधिरथिः संख्ये चेदिपाञ्चालपाण्डवान् ।\nएको बहूनभ्यपतद्गरुत्मन्पन्नगानिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Adhiratha's son alone fell on those many Chedis, Panchalas and Pandavas in the battle, as Garuda falls on snakes."}},{"n":69,"text":"भीमसेनस्तु संक्रुद्धः कुरून्मद्रान्सकेकयान् ।\nएकः संख्ये महेष्वासो योधयन्बह्वशोभत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhimasena, greatly angered, a great archer fighting alone in the battle, shone as he fought the Kurus, the Madras and the Kekayas."}},{"n":70,"text":"तत्र मर्मसु भीमेन नाराचैस्ताडिता गजाः ।\nप्रपतन्तो हतारोहाः कम्पयन्ति स्म मेदिनीम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"There elephants struck in their vital parts by Bhima's iron arrows, their riders slain, fell and made the earth shake."}},{"n":71,"text":"वाजिनश्च हतारोहाः पत्तयश्च गतासवः ।\nशेरते युधि निर्भिन्ना वमन्तो रुधिरं बहु ॥","meaning":{"en":"Horses with their riders slain and foot soldiers lifeless lay in the battle, torn open and vomiting much blood."}},{"n":72,"text":"सहस्रशश्च रथिनः पतिताः पतितायुधाः ।\nअक्षताः समदृश्यन्त भीमाद्भीता गतासवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thousands of charioteers, fallen and without weapons, were seen lying unwounded and lifeless, dead of fear of Bhima."}},{"n":73,"text":"रथिभिर्वाजिभिः सूतैः पत्तिभिश्च तथा गजैः ।\nभीमसेनशरच्छिन्नैरास्तीर्णा वसुधाभवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The earth was covered with charioteers, horses, drivers, foot soldiers and elephants cut down by Bhimasena's arrows."}},{"n":74,"text":"तत्स्तम्भितमिवातिष्ठद्भीमसेनबलार्दितम् ।\nदुर्योधनबलं राजन्निरुत्साहं कृतव्रणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Duryodhana's force, battered by Bhimasena's strength, stood as if frozen, wounded and without spirit."}},{"n":75,"text":"निश्चेष्टं तुमुले दीनं बभौ तस्मिन्महारणे ।\nप्रसन्नसलिलः काले यथा स्यात्सागरो नृप ॥","meaning":{"en":"Motionless and wretched in that tumult of the great battle, it looked, king, like the sea gone calm and clear at its season."}},{"n":76,"text":"मन्युवीर्यबलोपेतं बलात्पर्यवरोपितम् ।\nअभवत्तव पुत्रस्य तत्सैन्यमिषुभिस्तदा ।\nरुधिरौघपरिक्लिन्नं रुधिरार्द्रं बभूव ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"That army of your son, though full of anger, courage and strength, was brought down by force with arrows, and it became soaked, wet with floods of blood."}},{"n":77,"text":"सूतपुत्रो रणे क्रुद्धः पाण्डवानामनीकिनीम् ।\nभीमसेनः कुरूंश्चापि द्रावयन्बह्वशोभत ॥","meaning":{"en":"The charioteer's son, enraged in the battle, shone as he routed the Pandava army, and Bhimasena as he routed the Kurus."}},{"n":78,"text":"वर्तमाने तथा रौद्रे संग्रामेऽद्भुतदर्शने ।\nनिहत्य पृतनामध्ये संशप्तकगणान्बहून् ॥","meaning":{"en":"While that dreadful and marvellous battle went on, Arjuna, best of the victorious, having killed many troops of Samshaptakas in the midst of the army, spoke to Vasudeva."}},{"n":79,"text":"अर्जुनो जयतां श्रेष्ठो वासुदेवमथाब्रवीत् ।\nप्रभग्नं बलमेतद्धि योत्स्यमानं जनार्दन ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Janardana, this force of ours, which was ready to fight, has been broken."}},{"n":80,"text":"एते धावन्ति सगणाः संशप्तकमहारथाः ।\nअपारयन्तो मद्बाणान्सिंहशब्दान्मृगा इव ॥","meaning":{"en":"These great chariot-warriors of the Samshaptakas with their troops are running, unable to bear my arrows, like deer at the roar of a lion."}},{"n":81,"text":"दीर्यते च महत्सैन्यं सृञ्जयानां महारणे ।\nहस्तिकक्ष्यो ह्यसौ कृष्ण केतुः कर्णस्य धीमतः ।\nदृश्यते राजसैन्यस्य मध्ये विचरतो मुहुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The great army of the Srinjayas is being torn apart in the great battle. Krishna, there is the banner of wise Karna, marked with an elephant's rope, seen again and again as he moves in the midst of the king's army."}},{"n":82,"text":"न च कर्णं रणे शक्ता जेतुमन्ये महारथाः ।\nजानीते हि भवान्कर्णं वीर्यवन्तं पराक्रमे ॥","meaning":{"en":"No other great chariot-warriors are able to defeat Karna in the battle, and you know Karna to be strong in valour."}},{"n":83,"text":"तत्र याहि यतः कर्णो द्रावयत्येष नो बलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Go there, where Karna is routing our army."}},{"n":84,"text":"वर्जयित्वा रणे याहि सूतपुत्रं महारथम् ।\nश्रमो मा बाधते कृष्ण यथा वा तव रोचते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Go, passing by the charioteer's son, the great chariot-warrior, in the battle; fatigue troubles me, Krishna, or as it pleases you.\""}},{"n":85,"text":"एतच्छ्रुत्वा महाराज गोविन्दः प्रहसन्निव ।\nअब्रवीदर्जुनं तूर्णं कौरवाञ्जहि पाण्डव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing this, great king, Govinda, as if smiling, quickly said to Arjuna, \"Pandava, kill the Kauravas.\""}},{"n":86,"text":"ततस्तव महत्सैन्यं गोविन्दप्रेरिता हयाः ।\nहंसवर्णाः प्रविविशुर्वहन्तः कृष्णपाण्डवौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the swan-white horses, urged on by Govinda, entered your great army, carrying Krishna and Arjuna."}},{"n":87,"text":"केशवप्रहितैरश्वैः श्वेतैः काञ्चनभूषणैः ।\nप्रविशद्भिस्तव बलं चतुर्दिशमभिद्यत ॥","meaning":{"en":"As the white horses with golden ornaments, driven by Keshava, entered your force, it was split in the four directions."}},{"n":88,"text":"तौ विदार्य महासेनां प्रविष्टौ केशवार्जुनौ ।\nक्रुद्धौ संरम्भरक्ताक्षौ व्यभ्राजेतां महाद्युती ॥","meaning":{"en":"Keshava and Arjuna, those two of great splendour, angry and red-eyed with fury, tore through the great host, entered it and shone."}},{"n":89,"text":"युद्धशौण्डौ समाहूतावरिभिस्तौ रणाध्वरम् ।\nयज्वभिर्विधिनाहूतौ मखे देवाविवाश्विनौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Eager for battle and called out to by their enemies, the two came to that sacrifice of war, like the two Ashvins called by sacrificers to a rite with due ritual."}},{"n":90,"text":"क्रुद्धौ तौ तु नरव्याघ्रौ वेगवन्तौ बभूवतुः ।\nतलशब्देन रुषितौ यथा नागौ महाहवे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those two tigers among men, enraged, became swift, like two elephants maddened by the clap of a hand in the great battle."}},{"n":91,"text":"विगाहन्स रथानीकमश्वसंघांश्च फल्गुनः ।\nव्यचरत्पृतनामध्ये पाशहस्त इवान्तकः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Plunging into the chariot divisions and the masses of horses, Arjuna moved about the army like Death with a noose in hand."}},{"n":92,"text":"तं दृष्ट्वा युधि विक्रान्तं सेनायां तव भारत ।\nसंशप्तकगणान्भूयः पुत्रस्ते समचोदयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bharata, seeing him show his valour in the battle among your army, your son again urged on the troops of Samshaptakas."}},{"n":93,"text":"ततो रथसहस्रेण द्विरदानां त्रिभिः शतैः ।\nचतुर्दशसहस्रैश्च तुरगाणां महाहवे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, in the great battle, with a thousand chariots, three hundred elephants, fourteen thousand horses,"}},{"n":94,"text":"द्वाभ्यां शतसहस्राभ्यां पदातीनां च धन्विनाम् ।\nशूराणां नामलब्धानां विदितानां समन्ततः ।\nअभ्यवर्तन्त तौ वीरौ छादयन्तो महारथाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"and two hundred thousand foot archers, famous heroes known on every side, those great chariot-warriors came against the two heroes, covering them."}},{"n":95,"text":"स छाद्यमानः समरे शरैः परबलार्दनः ।\nदर्शयन्रौद्रमात्मानं पाशहस्त इवान्तकः ।\nनिघ्नन्संशप्तकान्पार्थः प्रेक्षणीयतरोऽभवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Covered with arrows in the battle, Arjuna, crusher of enemy forces, showing himself fearsome like Death with a noose in hand and killing the Samshaptakas, became even more worth looking at."}},{"n":96,"text":"ततो विद्युत्प्रभैर्बाणैः कार्तस्वरविभूषितैः ।\nनिरन्तरमिवाकाशमासीन्नुन्नैः किरीटिना ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the sky, driven by arrows of lightning brightness adorned with gold shot by Arjuna, seemed packed without a gap."}},{"n":97,"text":"किरीटिभुजनिर्मुक्तैः संपतद्भिर्महाशरैः ।\nसमाच्छन्नं बभौ सर्वं काद्रवेयैरिव प्रभो ॥","meaning":{"en":"Lord, everything shone covered by the great arrows that fell from Arjuna's arms, as if by the sons of Kadru, the snakes."}},{"n":98,"text":"रुक्मपुङ्खान्प्रसन्नाग्राञ्शरान्संनतपर्वणः ।\nअदर्शयदमेयात्मा दिक्षु सर्वासु पाण्डवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Pandava of immeasurable spirit showed arrows with golden feathers, bright points and bent joints in all the directions."}},{"n":99,"text":"हत्वा दश सहस्राणि पार्थिवानां महारथः ।\nसंशप्तकानां कौन्तेयः प्रपक्षं त्वरितोऽभ्ययात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having killed ten thousand of the warrior kings of the Samshaptakas, the great chariot-warrior Arjuna, son of Kunti, quickly went to the flank."}},{"n":100,"text":"प्रपक्षं स समासाद्य पार्थः काम्बोजरक्षितम् ।\nप्रममाथ बलाद्बाणैर्दानवानिव वासवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Reaching that flank, guarded by the Kambojas, Arjuna crushed it forcibly with arrows, as Indra crushed the Danavas."}},{"n":101,"text":"प्रचिच्छेदाशु भल्लैश्च द्विषतामाततायिनाम् ।\nशस्त्रपाणींस्तथा बाहूंस्तथापि च शिरांस्युत ॥","meaning":{"en":"With broad-headed arrows he swiftly cut off the hands that held weapons, the arms and the heads of those enemies who came to attack."}},{"n":102,"text":"अङ्गाङ्गावयवैश्छिन्नैर्व्यायुधास्तेऽपतन्क्षितौ ।\nविष्वग्वाताभिसंभग्ना बहुशाखा इव द्रुमाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"With their limbs and parts cut off, they fell to the ground unarmed, like many-branched trees broken by winds from every side."}},{"n":103,"text":"हस्त्यश्वरथपत्तीनां व्रातान्निघ्नन्तमर्जुनम् ।\nसुदक्षिणादवरजः शरवृष्ट्याभ्यवीवृषत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As Arjuna killed troops of elephants, horses, chariots and foot soldiers, the younger brother of Sudakshina rained a shower of arrows on him."}},{"n":104,"text":"अस्यास्यतोऽर्धचन्द्राभ्यां स बाहू परिघोपमौ ।\nपूर्णचन्द्राभवक्त्रं च क्षुरेणाभ्यहनच्छिरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As he shot, Arjuna cut off his two arms, like iron clubs, with two half-moon arrows, and struck his head, with a face like the full moon, with a razor-edged arrow."}},{"n":105,"text":"स पपात ततो वाहात्स्वलोहितपरिस्रवः ।\nमनःशिलागिरेः शृङ्गं वज्रेणेवावदारितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He fell from his mount, streaming blood, like the peak of a mountain of red arsenic split by a thunderbolt."}},{"n":106,"text":"सुदक्षिणादवरजं काम्बोजं ददृशुर्हतम् ।\nप्रांशुं कमलपत्राक्षमत्यर्थं प्रियदर्शनम् ।\nकाञ्चनस्तम्भसंकाशं भिन्नं हेमगिरिं यथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"They saw the Kamboja, younger brother of Sudakshina, slain: tall, lotus-eyed, very handsome to look at, like a golden pillar, like a golden mountain shattered."}},{"n":107,"text":"ततोऽभवत्पुनर्युद्धं घोरमद्भुतदर्शनम् ।\nनानावस्थाश्च योधानां बभूवुस्तत्र युध्यताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then again there was a fearful battle, wonderful to see, and the fighting warriors there were in many conditions."}},{"n":108,"text":"एतेष्वावर्जितैरश्वैः काम्बोजैर्यवनैः शकैः ।\nशोणिताक्तैस्तदा रक्तं सर्वमासीद्विशां पते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Lord of the people, with Kamboja, Yavana and Shaka horses wheeling about there, soaked in blood, everything became red."}},{"n":109,"text":"रथै रथाश्वसूतैश्च हतारोहैश्च वाजिभिः ।\nद्विरदैश्च हतारोहैर्महामात्रैर्हतद्विपैः ।\nअन्योन्येन महाराज कृतो घोरो जनक्षयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Great king, with chariots, horses and charioteers, horses whose riders were slain, elephants whose riders were slain, great mahouts and slain elephants, a terrible destruction of men was wrought by one another."}},{"n":110,"text":"तस्मिन्प्रपक्षे पक्षे च वध्यमाने महात्मना ।\nअर्जुनं जयतां श्रेष्ठं त्वरितो द्रौणिराययौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"While that flank and wing was being slaughtered by the great-souled Arjuna, best of the victorious, Ashvatthama quickly came up to him."}},{"n":111,"text":"विधुन्वानो महच्चापं कार्तस्वरविभूषितम् ।\nआददानः शरान्घोरान्स्वरश्मीनिव भास्करः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He shook his great bow adorned with gold and drew fearsome arrows, like the sun gathering its own rays."}},{"n":112,"text":"तैः पतद्भिर्महाराज द्रौणिमुक्तैः समन्ततः ।\nसंछादितौ रथस्थौ तावुभौ कृष्णधनंजयौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Great king, those arrows loosed by Ashvatthama, falling on every side, covered the two, Krishna and Dhananjaya, as they stood in their chariot."}},{"n":113,"text":"ततः शरशतैस्तीक्ष्णैर्भारद्वाजः प्रतापवान् ।\nनिश्चेष्टौ तावुभौ चक्रे युद्धे माधवपाण्डवौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the mighty son of Bharadvaja's line, with hundreds of sharp arrows, made both Madhava and the Pandava motionless in the battle."}},{"n":114,"text":"हाहाकृतमभूत्सर्वं जङ्गमं स्थावरं तथा ।\nचराचरस्य गोप्तारौ दृष्ट्वा संछादितौ शरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"All beings, moving and unmoving, cried out in distress, seeing the two protectors of the world of moving and unmoving things covered by arrows."}},{"n":115,"text":"सिद्धचारणसंघाश्च संपेतुर्वै समन्ततः ।\nचिन्तयन्तो भवेदद्य लोकानां स्वस्त्यपीत्यह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hosts of Siddhas and Charanas came together on every side, thinking, \"May it be well for the worlds today.\""}},{"n":116,"text":"न मया तादृशो राजन्दृष्टपूर्वः पराक्रमः ।\nसंजज्ञे यादृशो द्रौणेः कृष्णौ संछादयिष्यतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"King, I had never before seen a valour like that of Ashvatthama as he was about to cover the two Krishnas."}},{"n":117,"text":"द्रौणेस्तु धनुषः शब्दमहितत्रासनं रणे ।\nअश्रौषं बहुशो राजन्सिंहस्य नदतो यथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"King, I heard the sound of Ashvatthama's bow, which strikes terror in enemies, many times in the battle, like the roar of a lion."}},{"n":118,"text":"ज्या चास्य चरतो युद्धे सव्यदक्षिणमस्यतः ।\nविद्युदम्बुदमध्यस्था भ्राजमानेव साभवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As he moved in battle, shooting to left and to right, his bowstring shone as lightning in the midst of a cloud."}},{"n":119,"text":"स तथा क्षिप्रकारी च दृढहस्तश्च पाण्डवः ।\nसंमोहं परमं गत्वा प्रैक्षत द्रोणजं ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Pandava, though swift and firm of hand, fell into great bewilderment and gazed at the son of Drona."}},{"n":120,"text":"स विक्रमं हृतं मेने आत्मनः सुमहात्मना ।\nतथास्य समरे राजन्वपुरासीत्सुदुर्दृशम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He felt that his own valour had been taken away by that very great-souled man, and in the battle, king, Ashvatthama's body was hard to look at."}},{"n":121,"text":"द्रौणिपाण्डवयोरेवं वर्तमाने महारणे ।\nवर्धमाने च राजेन्द्र द्रोणपुत्रे महाबले ।\nहीयमाने च कौन्तेये कृष्णं रोषः समभ्ययात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"While the great battle between Ashvatthama and Arjuna went on thus, king of kings, with Drona's mighty son growing and Arjuna declining, anger came upon Krishna."}},{"n":122,"text":"स रोषान्निःश्वसन्राजन्निर्दहन्निव चक्षुषा ।\nद्रौणिं ह्यपश्यत्संग्रामे फल्गुनं च मुहुर्मुहुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sighing in anger, as if burning with his gaze, he looked at Ashvatthama in the battle and again and again at Arjuna."}},{"n":123,"text":"ततः क्रुद्धोऽब्रवीत्कृष्णः पार्थं सप्रणयं तदा ।\nअत्यद्भुतमिदं पार्थ तव पश्यामि संयुगे ।\nअतिशेते हि यत्र त्वा द्रोणपुत्रोऽद्य भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Krishna, angry, spoke lovingly to Arjuna: \"Arjuna, I see something very strange in this battle of yours: today Drona's son surpasses you."}},{"n":124,"text":"कच्चित्ते गाण्डिवं हस्ते रथे तिष्ठसि चार्जुन ।\nकच्चित्कुशलिनौ बाहू कच्चिद्वीर्यं तदेव ते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Is the Gandiva in your hand, and are you standing on your chariot? Are your arms well, and is your strength the same?\""}},{"n":125,"text":"एवमुक्तस्तु कृष्णेन क्षिप्त्वा भल्लांश्चतुर्दश ।\nत्वरमाणस्त्वराकाले द्रौणेर्धनुरथाच्छिनत् ।\nध्वजं छत्रं पताकां च रथं शक्तिं गदां तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Spoken to thus by Krishna, Arjuna, hurrying when haste was needed, shot fourteen broad-headed arrows and cut Ashvatthama's bow, his banner, umbrella, pennant, chariot, spear and mace."}},{"n":126,"text":"जत्रुदेशे च सुभृशं वत्सदन्तैरताडयत् ।\nस मूर्च्छां परमां गत्वा ध्वजयष्टिं समाश्रितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He struck him hard at the collarbone with calf-tooth arrows; Ashvatthama fainted deeply and leaned on his flagstaff."}},{"n":127,"text":"तं विसंज्ञं महाराज किरीटिभयपीडितम् ।\nअपोवाह रणात्सूतो रक्षमाणो धनंजयात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Great king, his charioteer, protecting him from Arjuna, carried him away from the battle, senseless and tormented by fear of Arjuna."}},{"n":128,"text":"एतस्मिन्नेव काले तु विजयः शत्रुतापनः ।\nन्यवधीत्तावकं सैन्यं शतशोऽथ सहस्रशः ।\nपश्यतस्तव पुत्रस्य तस्य वीरस्य भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"At that very time Vijaya, scorcher of foes, killed your army by the hundred and by the thousand, while your son, that hero, looked on, Bharata."}},{"n":129,"text":"एवमेष क्षयो वृत्तस्तावकानां परैः सह ।\nक्रूरो विशसनो घोरो राजन्दुर्मन्त्रिते तव ॥","meaning":{"en":"So this cruel, dreadful slaughter of your people by the enemy came about, king, through your bad counsel."}},{"n":130,"text":"संशप्तकांश्च कौन्तेयः कुरूंश्चापि वृकोदरः ।\nवसुषेणं च पाञ्चालः कृत्स्नेन व्यधमद्रणे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Arjuna wrecked the Samshaptakas in the battle, Vrikodara the Kurus, and Karna the Panchalas entirely."}}]}]}